MSXDEVStudio is free to download and use. In summary: make anything you like with
it, including commercial products, but do not sell MSXDEVStudio itself, and credit
the author in what you make.

By installing or using MSXDEVStudio you accept these terms.


1. PERMISSIONS

You may:

  a) Use MSXDEVStudio to create software of any kind, for any purpose, including
     commercial products. Whatever you create with MSXDEVStudio is entirely yours.
     The author claims no rights over your source code, your assets or your
     finished software, and no share of any revenue it earns.

  b) Copy and redistribute MSXDEVStudio itself, in its original unmodified form,
     provided you do so free of charge and keep this license and all copyright
     notices intact.

  c) Modify MSXDEVStudio for your own personal or internal use.

  d) Publish your modified source code so that it can be reviewed and
     contributed back: forking this repository, pushing a branch and opening a
     pull request are all expressly permitted, and encouraged. Contributions
     you submit to the project are offered under these same terms.


2. RESTRICTIONS

You may not:

  a) Sell MSXDEVStudio, charge any fee for access to it, or include it in a paid
     product, paid bundle, paid service or paid distribution. MSXDEVStudio must
     reach whoever receives it free of charge.

  b) Distribute modified builds of MSXDEVStudio — installers, packaged
     applications, or any other ready-to-run form — to end users without the
     author's written permission. Publishing modified source code under
     section 1(d) is always allowed; shipping a rival application built from it
     is not. This restriction applies to MSXDEVStudio itself, never to software
     you create with it.

  c) Remove, obscure or alter this license, the copyright notice, or the
     attribution required by section 3.


3. ATTRIBUTION

Software you create using MSXDEVStudio must credit the author. Use the wording:

    Built with MSXDEVStudio by P.D. Garaguso

or any similar wording that names the author. Place it somewhere a user can
reasonably find it: a title screen, a credits screen, an about box, a README
file, or accompanying documentation. This mirrors the attribution the MSXgl
library asks of the games built with it.

The credit must remain factual and neutral. It must not state or imply that
Pablo D. Garaguso endorses, sponsors, approves of, or is affiliated with your
software, nor may the author's name be used to promote it.


