MSXDEVStudio does not bundle or redistribute the MSX toolchain. MSXgl, the SDCC
compiler and the MSXtk tools are downloaded to the user's own machine by the
toolchain setup, and openMSX is installed separately by the user. Those
components remain under their own licenses, which are not affected by this
license and which you must comply with independently:

  MSXgl                       CC BY-SA 4.0
  MSXtk / MSXimg              CC BY-SA
  SDCC                        GNU General Public License
  ZX0                         BSD-3-Clause
  Bitbuster                   MIT-style
  Pletter                     free, informal terms
  openMSX                     GNU General Public License v2
  C-BIOS                      BSD-style
  WebMSX                      see that project

Components that ARE redistributed inside MSXDEVStudio's installers remain the
property of their respective authors, under the licenses shown:

  Electron, Vue, Pinia, Vue Router, the Monaco editor, chokidar, yauzl,
  xterm.js (@xterm/xterm, @xterm/addon-fit), node-pty (@lydell/node-pty)
                              MIT License
  Material Symbols (icon font)
                              Apache License 2.0 — full text in licenses/

The tutorials under docs/tutorials/ quote source code from the MSXgl sample
programs and are therefore licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0, matching MSXgl's own
license, rather than under the terms above.


